00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:21.839 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  over a year later Grand Theft Auto 5  remains one of the most consistently  entertaining video games I've ever  played  not to mention one of the most  convincing it takes on a shinier and  sharper 1080p form in its new home on  the PlayStation 4 but while it's visual  refinements are the most immediately  noticeable upgrade they're not the most  important partly that's because GTA 5 on  the Xbox 360 and PlayStation 3 looked  fantastic anyway even if the crisper  visuals here verge on the incredible at  times partly it's because there are a  host of new additions like vehicles guns  and songs but mostly it's because GTA 5  is almost an entirely different game or  it can be if you choose to play it a  certain way the new first-person mode  fundamentally changes not only how you  view GTA 5 world but your own mentality  towards it 4 while GTA has always been  violent sometimes shockingly so there's  always been something of a disconnect  between that violence and those playing  the game first-person mode removes much  of that disconnect so when I'm  mercilessly slaughtering police officers  in a high score bad or going on a  rampage with an RPG in downtown Los  Santos well I feel an easy yes there are  plenty of first-person shooters around  but few create as convincing a  modern-day setting as GTA does  first-person mode has the power to make  you stop and think about your actions  which is no bad thing in a game that's  long been criticized for glorifying a  life of crime rather than questioning it  the first person perspective feels very  different to that of your typical  shooter - it's slower and more measured  and well more lifelike the gentle head  bobs and animations as you leap over  walls or get carjacked on the highway  are all expertly done and really do draw  you into the game in a way that third  person mode never could the field of  view is also noticeably different with a  very cinematic wide-angle feel that  makes use of some nifty depth of field  effects if you play the excellent PT on  the PlayStation 4 you'll have a good  idea of what to expect here what  first-person is great for shooting and  for exploring a city that looks and  feels so much larger because of it  driving  work so well the twitchy hypersensitive  controls that work well in third person  for pulling off outrageous driving  stunts are just far too sensitive to get  the job done in first person I had to  drop the controller sensitivity down a  few notches just to keep cars on the  road trying to catch Michael son as he  dangles off a boat on the highway for  performing speeding drive-bys are very  difficult missions in the first person  which is arguably more realistic but I  found myself switching back to the third  person in order to get them done  thankfully it's not an either/or  situation and the game remembers your  preference on foot and in vehicles so  you don't have to manually switch  between the two even if you choose to  ignore first person completely GTA 5 has  lost little of its luster since release  this is a series that has consistently  been the most convincing and the most  cinematic in games even now I'm  surprised by just how much GTA nails it  the voice acting the scripting and the  dialogue are simply on another level  this helped create some credible if  wholly unlikable characters - but  perhaps that's the point there may be a  few times you sympathize with retired  gangster Michael as his family life  crumbles around him or when you believe  that wannabe gangster Franklin might be  a nice guy just because he says he's  always trying to do the right thing or  when Trevor  well maybe not travel but these are guys  that are not meant to be liked their  narcissistic psychopathic killers you  don't blink an eyelid at killing  hundreds when it serves their own means  they're not without fault - and there  are moments when a character will  contradict his own motivations seemingly  just to fit a mission structure but the  fact that these characters can be so  convincingly terrifying is a testament  to the great writing on show in GTA 5  that extends to the world at large - the  sprawling gorgeously animated metropolis  of Los Santos deftly satirizes its  real-world inspiration and of America as  a whole sure it's sometimes heavy-handed  but there are few games that would dare  go as far as GTA ders with his  commentary on governments media and  celebrities and fewer still that do it  with such conviction running through it  all are incredible bombastic missions  that play out like Hollywood  blockbusters and the finest of gangster  films heist remain the highlight and the  whole process of planning them out  hiring members of the team  gathering equipment and then hoping that  the fuzz doesn't interfere with them on  the big day is incredibly engrossing  bombs are exploded helicopters are  smashed into the side of skyscrapers an  entire squads of police give chase as  you attempt an escape down the highway  that's not to mention all the random  creeps of los santos who give you side  missions the multiple leisure activities  you can indulge in or the real estate  you can invest in and the stocks you can  buy in the markets you can manipulate or  you can just slack that all off  completely and use Los Santos as your  own wonderful digital playground  indeed it's the adventures that you  create yourself that often prove to be  the most fun  and then there's GTA online it's safe to  say GTA online can get off to a very  good start with server issues and all  manner of balance problems with the  all-new GTA 5 online gets a few boosts  including an enhanced character creator  as well as support for up to 30  simultaneous players  these are nice additions but the mode  still suffers from a lack of direction  at the start although you can import  your old one I opted to create a new  character after which I was dumped into  a sidewalk in Los Santos with little  idea of what I should do next once you  figure out the process of finding jobs  to do like stealing packages from NPCs  or taking part in street races and  people to do them with value or trusty  mobile phone things get more interesting  much has been said about how GTA online  is to open and how easy it is to be  killed by others but for me that's  always been part of its draw trolling  people who've taken themselves far too  seriously in a street race by creating  an epic roadblock still manages to raise  a smile suffice to say if you are hoping  for an epic reinvention of online you  won't find it here but even if online  wasn't part of the GTA 5 package it  wouldn't matter aside from a few mild  framerate issues that sometimes take the  edge off it's more dramatic moments GTA  5 is the bar by which all other  open-world games or indeed any game that  aims for a cinematic feel should be  judged it is beautiful  thought-provoking thrilling and an  incredible adventure from start to  finish even if you played through it  once already it's worth going back just  to be reminded of what an achievement  this game truly is  [Music]  [Music]

